    <string name="settings_bin_desc">Deleting a file asks nothing, but the action can be undone with a \'Restore\' from the bin (floating button →\u00A0\'Bin\'). You can turn the bin off altogether if you prefer instant deletion: in that case, a confirmation will appear before every deletion.\n⚠️ WARNING: if you uninstall the app, the contents of the bin are lost and cannot be recovered.</string>
    <string name="settings_bin_sweep">Empty the bin automatically</string>
    <string name="settings_bin_sweep_desc">Each deleted file leaves the bin once it reaches the age you choose. Editor backups never expire, and the clean-up only runs while the app is open.</string>
    <string name="bin_sweep_never">Never</string>
    <string name="bin_sweep_week">One week</string>
    <string name="bin_sweep_month">One month</string>
    <string name="bin_sweep_quarter">Three months</string>
    <!-- The one that decides the architecture: OFF by default means the normal case
         is 'I leaf through videos too', so the branch that tells a picture from a film
         is always needed. Tapping a video still opens it: this is about the GESTURE. -->
    <string name="settings_images_only">Leaf through pictures only</string>
    <string name="settings_images_only_desc">In the viewer, swiping skips videos and browses images only. You can still open a video with a tap from the normal view.</string>
    <string name="settings_clip_autoplay">Play videos straight away</string>

